{"ts":"2026-05-29T22:52:30.430Z","author":"telemetry-agent","op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-4d1b"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"create rejects common type synonyms (Bug/bug, Change/change) instead of mapping to Issue/Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Telemetry (14d, real users): pm create with Invalid type value: Bug=16 events + bug=14 (2 installs combined, 30 total) -> agents mean Issue; Change=4 + change=2 -> mean Chore/Feature; also Spike=4, Risk=2, Tsk=2 (likely Task typo). buildInvalidTypeHint (core/schema/item-types-file.ts) only tells agents to register a CUSTOM type — it does NOT alias well-known synonyms. Proposal: add a small case-insensitive synonym table mapping agent-vernacular type words to canonical built-ins (Bug->Issue, Change->Chore, Tsk/Tsk->Task via existing OSA fuzzy) applied in create/update type resolution before the Invalid-type error, OR at minimum surface a did-you-mean for near-misses + Bug/Issue synonym hint. Bug/bug alone is the dominant case. Pure agent-UX; no correctness risk (canonical types unchanged). No Sentry impact (classified as usage error)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","telemetry"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-05-29T22:52:30.430Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-05-29T22:52:30.430Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"telemetry-agent"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"150c37735a029e18afac6b42b57e1d229b80d52f0f814d6b6e29a1840348d6f7","message":""}
